  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U8", "U9"],
      "pins": ["U8.14", "U8.15", "U9.14", "U9.15"],
      "nets": ["CAN_CIPO", "CAN_COPI"],
      "observed": "On the CAN BUS sheet, the MCP2515 SPI slave data pins are wired with the net CAN_CIPO on the SI (slave-in / MOSI) pin and CAN_COPI on the SO (slave-out / MISO) pin (page 6 U8 pin14=CAN_CIPO, pin15=CAN_COPI; page 10 U9 pin14=CAN_CIPO, pin15=CAN_COPI).",
      "expected": "COPI (Controller Out / Peripheral In) is the master->slave data line and must connect to the slave's SI; CIPO (Controller In / Peripheral Out) is the slave->master line and must connect to the slave's SO. The board's own SPI Naming Note states 'COPI Controller Out, Peripheral In / CIPO Controller In, Peripheral Out', and the SC16IS752 UART expanders on the same SPI family are wired correctly (U13 pin11 SI=SERIAL_COPI, pin12 SO=SERIAL_CIPO). The CAN controllers therefore have MOSI and MISO swapped.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "CAN BUS sheet (page 6): U8 MCP2515-xSO, pin14 net label 'CAN_CIPO', pin15 net label 'CAN_COPI'"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "CAN BUS sheet (page 10): U9 MCP2515-xSO, pin14 'CAN_CIPO', pin15 'CAN_COPI'"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Serial sheet (page 8): U13 SC16IS752, pin11 A1/SI = SERIAL_COPI, pin12 SD = SERIAL_CIPO (correct reference)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "SPI Naming Note: COPI 'Controller Out, Peripheral In' CIPO 'Controller In, Peripheral Out'"}
      ],
      "impact": "The SPI bus to both CAN controllers is reversed: the controller's serial-out drives the master's serial-out and vice-versa. The MCP2515s cannot be configured or polled, so CAN0 and CAN1 never come up and the rover cannot communicate with the Odrive motor controllers over the isolated CAN buses.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The board matches the specification in its headline items (16 MHz crystals on Y1/Y2, LTC4412 ideal-diode U6, SN74LVC1G07 e-stop buffers, ISL54222AIUZ analog switch, WS2812 chain), but the SPI data lines to the two MCP2515 CAN controllers (U8/U9) appear swapped relative to the correctly-wired UART expanders, which would break CAN0/CAN1."
}

